<LegalDocument
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Carinya Digital collects, uses, and discloses personal information when you use our website, agent plugins, and services."
  effective="23 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how Carinya Digital ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and discloses
    personal information. It is written for the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
    Principles (APPs).
  </p>
  <p>
    It covers our website at carinyadigital.com, the agent plugins and other resources we publish,
    and professional services we provide, such as configuring Claude Cowork for a business. Our <a
      href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a
    > govern use of those services. This policy explains the
    personal-information side of that relationship.
  </p>
  <p>
    It does not cover personal information that an AI provider collects when you use their product.
    Claude is provided by Anthropic. ChatGPT is provided by OpenAI. Cursor is provided by Anysphere.
    When you use those products, including with one of our plugins installed, that provider's privacy
    policy applies to what you submit there. We do not operate those products, and our plugins do not
    send your prompts, files, or outputs to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    "Personal information" has the meaning given in the Privacy Act: information or an opinion about
    an identified individual, or an individual who is reasonably identifiable, whether or not the
    information is true, and whether or not it is recorded in a material form.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2>
  <p>This policy applies to personal information we collect from:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>visitors to our website</li>
    <li>people who email us or otherwise contact us</li>
    <li>clients of our professional services</li>
    <li>people who send us feedback about our resources</li>
  </ul>
  <p>It does not apply to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>information that is already public</li>
    <li>de-identified or aggregated information that does not identify anyone</li>
    <li>
      personal information an AI provider, GitHub, or another third party collects from you under
      their own policy
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Personal information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Contact details, such as your name, email address, and organisation, when you write to us or
      engage us.
    </li>
    <li>The contents of your correspondence with us.</li>
    <li>
      Details of a professional engagement, including the business context you choose to share so we
      can do the work.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payment information, if you pay us. Card or bank details are collected by the payment provider
      we use. We do not store full card numbers on our own systems.
    </li>
    <li>Feedback you choose to send about the website, a plugin, or a piece of work.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not ask you to create an account on this website.</p>

  <h3>Information collected when you use the website</h3>
  <p>When you visit the site, we or our service providers may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>device and browser details, such as browser type, operating system, and screen size</li>
    <li>connection details, such as IP address and the approximate location derived from it</li>
    <li>usage details, such as pages viewed, the time of the visit, and the site that referred you</li>
    <li>cookie and similar identifiers, described in section 7</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use this to run the site, understand which pages are useful, and diagnose faults.</p>

  <h3>Information we do not collect through plugins</h3>
  <p>
    Our agent plugins, practice plugins, and agent directories (including Waratah) are instructions
    and configuration. They run inside the AI product you choose. They are not a hosted service of
    ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Installing or running a plugin does not, by itself, send your prompts, files, outputs, or account
    contents to Carinya Digital. We do not use that material to train models. We do not buy personal
    information in order to train models. We do not operate a model.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you include personal information in a session with Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or a similar
    product, that provider collects it under its own privacy policy. You are responsible for having
    the rights and authority to submit that material, including where it is about someone else, such
    as a client of your practice.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a future resource sends data to us, we will say so in the resource and update this policy
    before we rely on it.
  </p>

  <h3>Information from a professional engagement</h3>
  <p>
    If we design, configure, or run agents for you, we collect the personal information you give us
    for that work. That can include business records, file extracts, and correspondence. We use it
    to carry out the engagement, to administer the relationship, and as this policy otherwise allows.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use personal information</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>answer enquiries and provide the services you ask for</li>
    <li>prepare quotes, invoices, and records of a professional engagement</li>
    <li>send messages the work requires, such as a confirmation or a draft for review</li>
    <li>
      send newsletters or similar updates where the Spam Act 2003 (Cth) allows it, and stop when you
      unsubscribe
    </li>
    <li>understand how the website is used and improve it</li>
    <li>protect the site and our services against misuse, fraud, and security incidents</li>
    <li>meet our legal, tax, and accounting obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information.</p>

  <h2>4. When we disclose personal information</h2>
  <p>We may disclose personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      service providers who host the website, deliver email, process payments, or measure traffic,
      and only so they can do that work for us
    </li>
    <li>professional advisers, such as lawyers and accountants</li>
    <li>
      a buyer or adviser in a sale or restructure of the business, under confidentiality obligations
    </li>
    <li>
      a regulator, court, or law-enforcement body where the law requires or authorises it, or where
      we reasonably believe disclosure is needed to prevent serious harm
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose personal information where you ask us to, or where you would reasonably
    expect it as part of the service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party AI products are not a disclosure by us. When you use Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or
    GitHub, you deal directly with that provider.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Agent plugins and third-party AI products</h2>
  <p>This section is here so it is easy to find if you are reviewing a plugin listing.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The plugins we publish are for use inside products we do not operate.</li>
    <li>
      Those products process your prompts, files, and outputs under their own terms and privacy
      policy. For Claude, that provider is Anthropic. For ChatGPT, it is OpenAI. For Cursor, it is
      Anysphere. GitHub hosts our source code under GitHub's own terms.
    </li>
    <li>
      Anthropic publishes its privacy policy and customer terms at <a
        href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal">anthropic.com/legal</a
      >. The Anthropic terms that
      apply depend on the kind of Claude account you hold.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do not control those providers, and we are not responsible for their privacy practices.
    </li>
    <li>
      Review the provider's policy before you connect files, inboxes, or other systems, and before
      you include personal information about clients or staff.
    </li>
    <li>
      Outputs are drafts. They can be wrong. We do not see them unless you send them to us.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Overseas disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers store or process information outside Australia, including in the
    United States and Europe. Where we disclose personal information to an overseas recipient, we
    take reasonable steps to ensure they handle it consistently with the APPs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Material you submit to an AI provider is handled under that provider's policy, which may involve
    storage outside Australia. That disclosure is yours, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use cookies and similar technologies where they are needed to run the site. We may also use a
    tag manager, such as Google Tag Manager, and analytics tools to count visits and see which pages
    are used. Those tools may set their own cookies and may process technical data outside Australia.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can set your browser to refuse cookies or to tell you when one is set. If you do, the site
    should still be readable. Some measurements will be less accurate.
  </p>
  <p>We do not use personal information to sell targeted advertising.</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect personal information from
    misuse, interference, loss, and unauthorised access, modification, or disclosure. Those steps
    include access controls on our own systems and encryption in transit (HTTPS) on the website.
  </p>
  <p>
    No internet transmission or storage is completely secure. Take care with what you send us, and
    avoid sending sensitive client files by ordinary email if a safer channel has been agreed.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we become aware of a data breach that is likely to result in serious harm, we will assess it
    and notify the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner and affected people where the
    Notifiable Data Breaches scheme requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. How long we keep personal information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purpose it was collected, or as
    long as the law requires. When we no longer need it, we delete it or de-identify it.
  </p>
