  <h2>10. Access, correction, and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for access to the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct it
    if it is inaccurate, out of date, incomplete, or misleading. You can also ask us to delete
    personal information we are not required to keep.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href="mailto:hello@carinyadigital.com">hello@carinyadigital.com</a>.
    We may need enough detail to confirm we are dealing with you, or with someone you have
    authorised. We will respond within a reasonable period, and in any case within 30 days. If we
    refuse a request, we will tell you why, unless the law says we should not, and how you can
    complain.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe we have handled personal information in a way that breaches the APPs, write to us
    first. We will acknowledge your complaint within 7 days and aim to resolve it within 30 days. If
    you are not satisfied, you can contact the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/"
      >Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    If another privacy law applies to you and gives you a further right, contact us and we will
    consider the request under that law.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our website, plugins, and services are not directed at children under 18. We do not knowingly
    collect personal information from a child under 18. If you believe we have, email us and we will
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. When we do, we will change the effective date at the top of this page.
    If a change is material, we will also note it on this page. The current version is the one
    published at carinyadigital.com/legal/privacy.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Carinya Digital<br />
    The Branch, New South Wales, Australia<br />
    <a href="mailto:hello@carinyadigital.com">hello@carinyadigital.com</a>
  </p>
  <p>Privacy questions, access requests, and complaints go to that address.</p>
</LegalDocument>
